      "code": "r = sc_asn1_decode(ctx, asn1_pubkey, *buf, *buflen, buf, buflen);",
      "note": "sc_asn1_decode consumes the attacker-controlled PoC buffer; during partial decoding, asn1_decode_entry allocates a heap buffer and stores it in obj->content.value (via the der alias). The call returns a negative error code because the PoC is a malformed PKCS#15 public key entry."
    },
    {
      "kind": "root_cause_function",
      "file": "src/libopensc/pkcs15-pubkey.c",
      "function": "sc_pkcs15_decode_pukdf_entry",
      "line": null,
      "code": "",
      "note": "On sc_asn1_decode error (r < 0), the error handler calls free(der->value) which frees obj->content.value, but does not null the pointer or zero obj->content.len. The dangling pointer persists in obj->content, enabling the caller's cleanup to free it a second time. The fix (commit 5557f34) removes this premature free entirely."
    },
